From: elish-linux-tuning contributors
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] ASoC: cs35l41: poll raw IRQ1 status and tolerate boost timeout in cs35l41_global_enable

On Xiaomi Mi Pad 5 Pro (xiaomi-elish) running Linux 6.18, the 8x CS35L41
amplifiers use internal boost (CS35L41_INT_BOOST). In cs35l41_global_enable():
1. Polling CS35L41_IRQ1_STATUS1 (0x10010) never observes CS35L41_PUP_DONE_MASK
   because the interrupt is masked; polling CS35L41_IRQ1_RAW_STATUS1 (0x10090)
   reads the unmasked hardware status.
2. If PUP_DONE still times out (-ETIMEDOUT / -110), returning the error aborts
   DAPM and keeps all 8 speakers silent. Logging the warning and resetting
   ret = 0 allows audio playback to proceed.

Target file: sound/soc/codecs/cs35l41-lib.c (function cs35l41_global_enable)

---
 sound/soc/codecs/cs35l41-lib.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l41-lib.c b/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l41-lib.c
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l41-lib.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l41-lib.c
@@ -1120,11 +1120,13 @@ int cs35l41_global_enable(struct device *dev, struct regmap *regmap, enum cs35l4
 			return ret;
 		}
 
-		ret = regmap_read_poll_timeout(regmap, CS35L41_IRQ1_STATUS1,
+		ret = regmap_read_poll_timeout(regmap, CS35L41_IRQ1_RAW_STATUS1,
 					       val, val & CS35L41_PUP_DONE_MASK,
 					       1000, 100000);
-		if (ret)
+		if (ret) {
 			dev_err(dev, "PUP_DONE not set: %d\n", ret);
+			ret = 0;
+		}
 		break;
 	case CS35L41_EXT_BOOST:
 	case CS35L41_EXT_BOOST_NO_VSPK_SWITCH:
-- 
2.43.0
